  "description": "Point Odyssey annotation corrections. In the affected sequences the extrinsics array is offset by one frame relative to the rendered images: extrinsics[t] is the pose that rendered frame t-1, while trajs_3d[t] is correctly indexed. Because trajs_2d == project(extrinsics @ trajs_3d), the 2D tracks drift off their object by f_px * theta pixels -- negligible when the camera is slow, several hundred pixels during a fast camera rotation. Repair: read camera arrays at t + cam_offset and recompute trajs_2d from them; invalidate the trailing frames that have no counterpart. visibs and trajs_3d are left unmodified.",
